==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|liecht|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|lioht|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*leuhtaz}}, ultimately from the {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} root {{term/t|ine-pro|*lewk-}}. Compare Dutch {{term|licht|lang=nl}}, English ''[[light]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-at-Licht.ogg|audio (Austria)}}
* {{IPA|/lɪçt/|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|ɪçt|lang=de}}

===Adjective===
{{head|de|adjective}}

# [[light]], [[bright]] (luminescent)
# [[unobstructed]], [[clear]]
#: ''Du hast da eine '''lichte''' Stelle.'' - You have an almost bald spot.

====Related terms====
* [[Licht]] {{n}}

