===Etymology===
From {{etyl|de|hrx}} {{term|Licht||lang=de}}, from {{etyl|goh|hrx}} {{term|lioht|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|hrx}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*leuhtą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|hrx}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*lewk-||bright, to shine, to see}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/lɪxt/|lang=hrx}}

===Noun===
{{head|hrx|noun|g=n}}

# [[light]]
#* Bible, Genesis 1:5
#*: Kot hot es '''licht''' "taach" kenënt un tii tunkelheet "naacht" kenënt.
#*:: God called the '''light''' "day", and the darkness he called "night".

====Antonyms====
* [[tunkelheet]]

====Related terms====
* [[lichte]], [[lichten]]

